[0.101, "o", "miu-cr: 04:17:55.665 reviewing 1 files (1 changed)…\r\n"]
[0.048, "o", "miu-cr: 04:17:55.714 thinking… (turn 1)\r\n"]
[17.021, "o", "miu-cr: 04:18:12.735 done: 1 findings\r\n\u001b[31m\u001b[1m✖ CRITICAL (security)\u001b[0m  \u001b[36mapi/admin.go:7-9\u001b[0m\r\n    Removing the `return` after `http.Error` does not stop handler execution, so `w.Write([]byte(secretReport()))` runs for every request, including non-admins. `http.Error` only sets the 403 status and body; it returns no control flow. Any unauthenticated or non-admin caller now receives the secret report appended after the \"forbidden\" message, which is an auth bypass with direct data disclosure. Restore the early return.\r\n  \u001b[2mcode:\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m│ if !isAdmin(r) {\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m│ \t\thttp.Error(w, \"forbidden\", http.StatusForbidden)\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m│ \t}\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2msuggested patch:\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m│ \tif !isAdmin(r) {\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m│ \t\thttp.Error(w, \"forbidden\", http.StatusForbidden)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "    \u001b[2m│ \t\treturn\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m│ \t}\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n1 finding(s):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  critical 1\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "exit=2\r\n"]
[6.014, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[3J"]
[0.001, "o", "\u001b[2m# 3. every review is saved\u001b[0m\r\n"]
